/examples/**/bin
*.test
*.out
/.native-build/

# rapid writes a timestamped fail file next to a failing property; useful while
# reproducing, not worth committing.
#
# The pattern needs the ** because a pattern containing a slash is anchored to
# the directory holding the .gitignore: plain "testdata/rapid/" matched only a
# top-level one, and the only module that uses rapid is properties/, so it
# covered nothing. Three .fail files reached a commit before this was noticed.
**/testdata/rapid/
.fuzzchain/
